    <string name="settings_help_title">Help</string>
    <string name="settings_help_a11y_q">Why is accessibility needed?</string>
    <string name="settings_help_a11y_a">The accessibility service improves the experience. With it on, the filter is drawn on a layer above regular windows and can cover the whole system (Settings, permission dialogs and other blocked screens) - something the normal overlay can\'t do, even with ADB or Shizuku. It also prevents the overlay from being closed or attacked by other system apps or by the system itself. The app does not read or collect screen content.</string>
    <string name="settings_help_random_q">Why does the filter turn off out of nowhere?</string>
    <string name="settings_help_random_a">Some devices (mainly TVs) have bloatware or system apps that close regular floating windows, or the system itself drops them. To fix this, Blood Moon needs the accessibility permission. If you don\'t want to grant it, or you did and an app still interferes, report the problem on the project\'s GitHub or find that app and remove it at your own risk - Diagnostics helps identify it.</string>

